// WEC-823 · type-check the Netlify functions.
//
// Until 22/09 `npm run typecheck` ran `tsc -b`, which follows tsconfig.json →
// tsconfig.app.json ("include": ["src"]) and tsconfig.node.json
// ("include": ["vite.config.ts"]). NOTHING under netlify/ was ever checked.
//
// That is the whole server: submit-order, the Viva payment libs, markPaid, the
// Airtable push, every menu endpoint. A green typecheck said nothing about any
// of them, and a change to one could be reported as "clean" having never been
// compiled. tsconfig.airtablecheck.json covered six files by hand; this covers
// all of them.
//
// Not wired into tsconfig.json's "references" on purpose: `tsc -b` wants
// referenced projects to be composite (declaration emit), which these are not
// and do not need to be. It runs as its own `tsc -p` step in the script.
//
// ── BASELINE, measured 22/09/2026: 29 errors ──────────────────────────────
// All pre-existing — this config introduced none of them. Use it the way the
// src side is already used: diff against origin/dev and ship only if no NEW
// error appears. The count is not zero and should not be treated as a gate.
//
// 15 of the 29 come from ONE missing dependency: `@netlify/functions` is
// imported by 9 functions but is not in package.json at all (9 × TS2307
// "cannot find module", cascading into 6 × TS7006 implicit-any on `event`).
// It is a types-only import, erased at runtime, which is why the functions
// work in production and nobody noticed. Adding it as a devDependency clears
// those 15 and needs a real `npm install` + lockfile change — deliberately NOT
// done here so this change stays config-only.
//
// The remaining 14 are genuine: Supabase client generic mismatches in
// admin-import-menu and verifyWalletPlanTransaction, an unsafe cast in
// menu-week, and a few implicit anys.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "target": "es2022",
    "lib": ["es2022", "dom"],
    // vite/client alongside node: functions import from src/ (e.g. the shared
    // supabase client), and those files read import.meta.env. Without it, three
    // errors appear in src/ that have nothing to do with the functions.
    "types": ["node", "vite/client"],
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true
  },
  "include": ["netlify/**/*.ts"]
}
